    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` rule: the create request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner exposes `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n**Key subtlety:** the `OwnerMapper` has an unqualified `String\u2192String` default method (`normalizeLine`) that MapStruct auto-applies to *every* plain String property, upper-casing `firstName`/`lastName`/`city` (via `AddressNormalizer`) before the entity is ever persisted. So a na\u00efve `getSalutation()` computed from the stored `lastName` yields `DR WHO`, not the expected `DR who`. The fix composes the salutation from the **raw** DTO values (original casing) at map time and reads it back with an explicit expression that bypasses the auto-applied normalizer.\n\nChanges, kept small and cohesive:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (input) to `OwnerFields` and read-only `salutation` to `Owner`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 `title` as a `@Transient` field and `salutation` as a persisted `@Column`, each with a plain getter/setter (no logic added to existing methods).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one explicit `@Mapping` on read (`owner.getSalutation()`, bypassing `normalizeLine`) and one on write composing from raw `title`/`lastName` via a new 1-line `composeSalutation` default method. No existing method bodies changed.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `salutation` column (the hsqldb dialect is the one kept in sync with the entity and used by the tests).\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.\n\nOne note for your awareness (not something I changed): the broad upper-casing of `firstName`/`lastName`/`city` is a pre-existing side effect of MapStruct auto-selecting `normalizeLine` for all String fields. I left it untouched to avoid disturbing established behavior, and worked around it rather than \"fixing\" it.",
